ectively a dvd educating them on how  they ought to be handling  uh passengers  that fall under that category and the  uh there's no sort of um assessment  of sorts on that the uh  we do have um  there are separate issues around  wheelchair access deliberately built  wheelchair accessible vehicles  and there is a separate requirement that  anybody driving one of them should have  had appropriate training in loading  the wheelchairs into the vehicle  right thank you so so they they know  that there's a  correct way which is um frontal back and  not  sideways then and that kind of  thing and the different ways that they  can be shuttled down  that's all included in in the knowledge  and the training then that's given  to the drivers is it in terms of  vehicles that are  especially adapted for wheelchairs then  yes they would be expected to have  undergone training on making sure that  they can safely  uh load and unload passengers and secure  them for travel  right and what about the ramps are they  allowed to use  um two single ramps  to get a person or does it have to be a  block  uh rams please i've got to be honest i'd  have to find out i don't know the answer  to that question i don't know what the  the regulations require um  i'd have to ask yeah okay okay thank you  just running through my thoughts when i  was reading it thank you  oops michelle would you like to  yeah chair if i may assist there it  would depend  on the type of ramp which is um  part of the vehicle they can vary from  vehicle to vehicle so we don't have a  specific  ramp type but they do vary according to  the types of vehicles that they  are uh that their purpose built for or  have been adapted for  so hopefully that will um answer cancer  councillor wendell's question yeah  some drivers or in the past they used to  have a  a sort of a separate ramp not with the  drop down  tail and i have come across problems  where they  sort of come along with two separate  um ramps which is okay there's n